Package: cetzDevice
Type: Package
Title: A 'CeTZ' Graphics Device for R
Version: 0.5.3.1
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Andrew Junhao", family = "Wu",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "andrew.junhao.wu@gmail.com"),
    person("Charlie", "Sharpsteen", role = "ctb",
        comment = "Adapted validation scenarios and manual layout"),
    person("Cameron", "Bracken", role = "ctb",
        comment = "Adapted validation scenarios and manual layout"))
Description: A graphics device that translates R graphics engine operations
    into editable 'CeTZ' source for 'Typst' documents. Supports base and 'grid'
    graphics, with 'Typst' text measurement, rectangular clipping,
    transparency, compound paths, embedded raster images, native 'Typst' and
    'MiTeX' labels, reusable text metrics, annotations, vector gradient fills,
    and multiple pages.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: digest, graphics, grDevices, grid, jsonlite, png, utils
Suggests: ggplot2, knitr, lattice, patchwork, systemfonts, testthat (>= 3.1.8)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
URL: https://github.com/SchrodingerBlume/cetzDevice
BugReports: https://github.com/SchrodingerBlume/cetzDevice/issues
SystemRequirements: Typst CLI (>= 0.15.0) for Typst font metrics;
    CeTZ 0.5.3 for compiling exported figures; MiTeX 0.2.6 for LaTeX labels
NeedsCompilation: yes
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/cetzDevice/CeTZ: 0.5.3
Config/cetzDevice/Typst: 0.15.0
